schema: public-use-boundary
object:
  title: Boundary — cultural/Indigenous attribution in the 5P gathering framework (gatherings-pattern.md)
  tier: public-with-caveat
  consent_note: >-
    The article attributes small-group-before-large-group decision patterns
    and Circle Practice's talking-piece format to "many East African
    communities" and "many African and Indigenous traditions" without naming
    a specific community or citing a community-authored source. This is a
    secondary, broad-strokes attribution from a toolkit article, not sourced
    directly from the communities named. Do not present as authoritative
    ethnographic claim; seek community-sourced or specialist review before
    republishing in a context that speaks on behalf of those traditions.
  review_type: domain-review-before-public-use
  notes: >-
    Covers the concept-lineage entry "Purpose-People-Place-Process-Practice
    (5P gathering framework)" (same work order) — flagged per the ingest
    skill's TEK/Indigenous-knowledge high-risk trigger.
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
